  "severity": "high",
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "CFG-001",
      "location": "apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/config.ts",
      "description": "turnTimeoutMs reduced from 45,000 ms (45 s) to 5,000 ms (5 s). A 5-second window is impractically short for a player turn: it does not account for network latency, UI interaction time, or strategic decision-making. This will cause frequent forced/auto-turns, player frustration, and potential mid-action state corruption if a timeout fires while the player is mid-input.",
      "risk": "Likely a typo (e.g., intended 50_000 but dropped a zero / misplaced the underscore). As-is, it breaks the core gameplay loop for every user."
    }
  ],
  "safe_fix": "Revert the value to the previous 45_000. If the intent was to *increase* the timeout to 50 s, use 50_000. Either way, validate the value against the product spec for turn duration before merging.\n\n  // apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/config.ts\n  turnTimeoutMs: 45_000,  // ← restore original (or 50_000 if 50 s is the intended new value)\n\nAdditionally, add a unit/integration test that asserts turnTimeoutMs is within a reasonable range (e.g., ≥ 10_000) to catch similar regressions in the future."
}
